// osprey: flavor=ml
// ML-flavor must-reject. Pins [DOC-SIGIL-INNER] (docs/specs/language/0026-DocumentationComments.md) and the
// cross-flavor half of [FLAVOR-LOWER-CONTRACT] (docs/specs/language/0023-LanguageFlavors.md).
//
// The inner sigil is spelled `//!` in BOTH flavors — only the outer sigil
// differs (`///` versus `(** … *)`). The ML frontend therefore rejects a `//!`
// that opens no scope exactly as the Default frontend does, and says so in
// words rather than dropping the documentation on the floor.

answer = 42

//! This documents nothing: no scope opens here.

print "${answer}"
